  },
  question: "Where do the hand-written grain witnesses end up? They test the declaration-grain realization from the host side and today live as hand-written Rust beside generated code in the stage0 mirror. The deferral names lane node adhoc-0eedbb6e-a35 and this tracking row: at enrollment the node either moves the witnesses into generated .dag test sources or records them as a standing hand-written exception with a receipt comment at the file, so no hand-written block in the mirror remains unaccounted.",
